preConditionHook:
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtRank -- Grimes A list (G08-02, key
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtRank; also G10-05, key StopInsideTestedSwingExtreme,
// merge decision 25). Authored 2026-09-22 as new inputs on
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry and split out 2026-11-07, because the 202611 BRK
// and OWN templates place InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry, so that rule stays
// exactly as those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged.
//
// DEFAULTS: pivotIndex(2) and stopLookback(20) are the merged candidate's values
// -- the penultimate pivot, with the pivot window widened so the scan can reach
// it; pivotStrength(2) and stopTicks(1) are InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry's own.
// At pivotIndex 1 and stopLookback 10 this is InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry's
// behaviour exactly.
//
// GUARD (2026-09-17): a level's EXISTENCE is a COUNT of pivots the scan found,
// never a test of the price against -1 -- a back-adjusted series can print
// -1.00 (or 0.00) as a real price. The EL twin counts the same way. Mentions of
// the -1 SENTINEL below describe what EL's SwingLow / SwingHigh return, not how
// this rule guards it.
// RISK TO THE SWING THAT EXISTED WHEN THE TRADE WAS TAKEN, AND LEAVE THE STOP
// THERE. The pivotIndex-th most recent confirmed swing low is captured on the
// fill bar and the level never moves again; Brooks's stop for limit-order
// channel entries.
//
// Kept apart from SwingPointTrailingStop, which re-reads the pivot every bar: on
// a trend that runs, the trailed rule exits far higher, and on a trend that never
// prints a new pivot the two are identical. Not StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry
// either, whose level is a running extreme that WIDENS as the trade goes against
// it, where this one is fixed at entry.
//
// THE LEVEL IS CAPTURED ON ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0 -- VERIFIED as 0 on the fill
// bar and as restarting through a reversal, which a ctx.MarketPosition() == 0
// reset would miss because a reversal never passes through flat. It is the same
// at-entry capture convention StopAtSignalBarRangeMultiple and
// PullbackSizedProfitTarget use, and it is what holds "reaches back" at the pivot
// window rather than at the length of the longest trade.
//
// THE PIVOT FORM IS USED, NOT THE lowest-low-over-stopLookback PROXY the source
// offers: the swing primitive is now MEASURED, so the proxy buys nothing.
// stopLookback is therefore the PIVOT WINDOW (EL's Length) rather than a lowest-low
// length -- at the source's 10 with strength 2 the reportable offsets are 2..9;
// at this rule's default 20 they are 2..19.
//
// TWO GRIMES READINGS, one rule.
//
// (1) pivotIndex (G08-02, key InitialStopBeyondSwingAtRank). "It is possible to
// step back to the penultimate pivot, with the trade-off of a much smaller
// position size." pivotIndex 2, the default, steps the stop back to the pivot
// before the most recent one, a wider stop much less likely to be hit; at
// pivotIndex 1 the level is InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry's. THE SCAN IS THE
// THREE-PIVOT FORM SwingPivotTarget ALREADY CARRIES, because the register lists
// SwingLow / SwingHigh Occurrence 3+ as UNMEASURED -- the deeper ranks are found
// by hand rather than by a third-occurrence call, pivotIndex is CLAMPED to the
// three pivots the scan keeps, and there is no early break, so the scan can
// reach them. The equivalence at pivotIndex 1 is BEHAVIOURAL, not textual: the
// first pivot found scanning newest-first is the same bar
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry's scan, which breaks at the first pivot,
// returns. The EL twin spells the same hand-rolled scan where
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry calls SwingLow(1, ...) / SwingHigh(1, ...), the
// equivalence SwingPivotTarget and ThreePushPattern already rest on. stopLookback
// has to widen with pivotIndex so the scan can reach the deeper pivot, which is
// why its default is 20 here against 10 there.
//
// (2) stopTicks IS SIGNED (merge decision 25, key StopInsideTestedSwingExtreme,
// G10-05). On a failure test Grimes deliberately inverts the usual convention and
// puts the stop AT or just INSIDE the tested extreme, ahead of the crowd's stop
// cluster: "a few extra premature stop-outs bought in exchange for much less
// slippage on the exits that matter." Mechanically that is a NEGATIVE stopTicks,
// so the grid runs below zero; the precedent is SwingHighProfitTarget.offsetTicks.
// It needed NO code change -- the arithmetic was already signed in
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry -- so this reading is equally a grid on that
// rule, and it is not what this one was split out for. The default stays at 1,
// the beyond-the-extreme reading. The long stop rises ABOVE the pivot
// and the short stop falls BELOW it, which is the correct mirror.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from SwingHigh per the B-list decision. MEASURED
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot test is
// MIXED -- at-or-beyond the pivotStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY beyond the
// pivotStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER index the
// NEWER bar, so the strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is
// exactly pivotStrength bars, never 0 or 1, so during the lag the PREVIOUS pivot
// is captured and nothing looks ahead; stopLookback is EL's Length, offsets
// 0..stopLookback-1 inclusive, and the neighbourhood test reaches pivotStrength
// bars PAST the window, so the deepest bar touched is
// stopLookback - 1 + pivotStrength; an empty window returns the -1 SENTINEL, and
// the pivot COUNTS are how it is guarded -- a captured -1 as a PRICE sits under
// every real price; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance,
// hence el_lt / el_le / el_gt / el_ge. The low side's tie sense is the mirror of
// the measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
// The scan runs unconditionally every bar, not only at entry, so Max Bars Back
// covers it and the EasyLanguage twin advances on the same bars.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// stopTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), into a local.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
for (jj = (int)pivotStrength; jj <= (int)stopLookback - 1; ++jj) {
    okHi = true;
    okLo = true;
    for (kk = jj - (int)pivotStrength; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + (int)pivotStrength; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) hiPx1 = high[jj];
        if (nHiPiv == 2) hiPx2 = high[jj];
        if (nHiPiv == 3) hiPx3 = high[jj];
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) loPx1 = low[jj];
        if (nLoPiv == 2) loPx2 = low[jj];
        if (nLoPiv == 3) loPx3 = low[jj];
    }
}
needP = (int)pivotIndex;
if (needP < 1) needP = 1;
if (needP > 3) needP = 3;
hi1 = hiPx3;
lo1 = loPx3;
if (needP == 1) { hi1 = hiPx1; lo1 = loPx1; }
if (needP == 2) { hi1 = hiPx2; lo1 = loPx2; }
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    haveStopLong = (nLoPiv >= needP);
    stopLong = lo1;
    haveStopShort = (nHiPiv >= needP);
    stopShort = hi1;
}
